            <ArticleTitle>In Vivo Analysis of Hypertension: Induction of Hypertension, In Vivo Kinase Manipulation, and Assessment of Physiologic Outputs.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>421-432</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/978-1-4939-6625-7_32</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Using an in vivo model system to study signal transduction will include several steps: (1) induce hypertension in the animal, (2) manipulate kinase activation and signal transduction pathways as desired, and (3) observe physiologic outputs. This chapter provides the reader with overviews of the techniques our lab uses to manipulate signal transduction pathways and determine the effects on hypertension.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
